# trembita documentation

## No reference projects

Do **not** name, link, or allude to external product apps, customer codebases, or private reference implementations in trembita documentation.

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
AcmeCorp's gateway port proved that most routes are data.
Real product apps serve as migration targets.
export TREMBITA_STATIC_ADMIN_BUCKET=acme-fe-admin

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
Large route tables (100+ routes) are mostly declarative data.
Validate conventions via examples/ and integration tests in this repo.
export TREMBITA_STATIC_ADMIN_BUCKET=my-app-fe-admin
```

Use only **in-repo** illustrations:

- `examples/` and `showcase/`
- crate APIs, tests, and scripts under this workspace
- generic placeholders (`my-app`, `api.example.com`, `my-app-fe-admin`)

Decision records describe **current** trembita design — not third-party adoption timelines or out-of-repo parity tooling.

## Pre-1.0 (no history narrative)

Until **1.0**, docs describe **what to do now**, not what changed between `0.x` releases:

- No version-to-version migration guides ([docs/README.md](../../docs/README.md))
- No detailed [CHANGELOG.md](../../CHANGELOG.md) entries (archive only: [docs/archive/](../../docs/archive/))
- ADRs: problem + decision + consequences — avoid “removed in 0.x”, “breaking from 0.y”, and old-vs-new comparison tables unless essential to the decision
- Prefer **ops HTTP** / **`TREMBITA_LISTEN`** over separate “admin port” or third-party router names; backlog items describe shipped [`RouteTable`](../crates/trembita-http/src/routing/table.rs) APIs, not removed stacks
